    "standards": {
      "title": "Editorial standards",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "page-heading",
          "visible": true,
          "settings": {
            "eyebrow": "Editorial standards",
            "heading": [
              "How we research",
              "and what we publish"
            ],
            "intro": "The rules every portfolio and article on World Art Review follows."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text",
          "type": "long-text",
          "visible": true,
          "settings": {
            "body": "<h2>Every fact has a source</h2>\n<p>Each fact in an artist portfolio carries a numbered citation to where it came from. If we cannot source something, we do not state it as fact; it appears as a gap to be filled.</p>\n<h2>We say who said it</h2>\n<p>We label sources by type: independent reporting, interviews with the artist, the artist's or gallery's own publicity, and gallery records. A claim that comes only from publicity is marked <span class=\"reported\">Reported</span>.</p>\n<h2>We show what is missing</h2>\n<p>Portfolios show a research status: how many facts are sourced and how many dates or details are still awaiting confirmation.</p>\n<h2>Our relationships</h2>\n<p><span class=\"placeholder\">Coming Soon</span></p>\n<h2>Corrections</h2>\n<p>If you spot an error, write to <a href=\"mailto:info@grovegallery.com?subject=Correction\">info@grovegallery.com</a>. We correct promptly and note the change on the page.</p>\n<h2>Privacy and terms</h2>\n<p><span class=\"placeholder\">[Privacy notice and terms of use to be added before launch.]</span></p>"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
